West Northamptonshire Council (WNC) is looking for suppliers who are interested in the following services on behalf of WNC and North Northamptonshire Council (NNC):

A:	Supplier 1 - for Hospital Body Storage, viewing room and all associated post-mortem facilities co-located on the same site, which is accessible 24hours a day, 7 days a week across WNC; &amp;

Supplier 2 - for Hospital Body Storage, viewing room and all associated post-mortem facilities co-located on the same site, which is accessible 24hours a day, 7 days a across NNC.

B:	Supplier 1 - for Transportation of Bodies for Northamptonshire Coroners Service. The supplier will need to manage the day to day collections and removals within 1 hour but must be available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week following a death in the community, and in addition be able to respond to support Northamptonshire Coroners Service in the event of Excess Deaths or a Mass Fatality across NNC: &amp;
	Supplier 2 - for Transportation of Bodies for Northamptonshire Coroners Service. The supplier will need to manage the day to day collections and removals within 1 hour but must be available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week following a death in the community, and in addition be able to respond to support Northamptonshire Coroners Service in the event of Excess Deaths or a Mass Fatality across WNC

West Northamptonshire Council (WNC) would like to invite you to an information event about our proposed Home Care provision from 2023/24.

The event will include the following information:
•	Broad outline of the proposed model;
•	Indicative timelines for the proposed recommissioning of Homecare;
•	Estimated volumes of activity within West Northamptonshire;
•	How you can register to tender and pre prepare for the proposed recommissioning.

However, we will not be discussing anything to do with, or answering any questions on:
•             Pricing;
•             Fair Cost of Care.

We will not have a Question and Answer session at the event due to timescales, however questions are able to be submitted via email to justine.horrocks@westnorthants.gov.uk and a Q&amp;A document will subsequently be sent out to all attendees following the event.

The event will take place via Microsoft Teams and will be held on Tuesday 29th November at 10.30am.

To attend this event, please email justine.horrocks@westnorthants.gov.uk no later than Friday 25th November to receive the Microsoft Teams information.

West Northamptonshire Council (WNC) is a new Unitary authority that came into existence on Thursday, 1st April 2021 following the Northamptonshire Structural Changes Order 2019. 

The primary purpose of this expression of interest (EOI) is to inform the market of a prospective opportunity and to seek feedback in relation to the requirement as set out below: 

The Authority have introduced a multi-agency quality assurance framework to assist with ensuring consistency within the quality of Education Health and Care Plans (EHCP&#039;s) and have now identified that a smarter way of carrying out multi-agency quality audits is required using an IT based tool. The tool needs to inform our actions for improvement and to measure the impact of these actions. The Provider must be able to demonstrate from recent experience over time measurable delivery of an Education Health Care Plan Quality Assurance Tool and the tool must be able to deliver against each point outlined below:
 
•	A developed and proven IT based tool that supports quality assurance of EHCPs and advice;
•	A tool that is based on recognised good practice and support implementation of the SEND Code of Practice;
•	Evidence of positive and sustained impact of use of this tool in other Local Areas; 
•	A tool that works with existing case management systems;
•	A tool that supports multi agency working, including with parents/ carers and young people (co-production practices);
•	A tool that can help us to benchmark improvement against other Local Areas;
•	A tool that will support us in making the best practice common practice in our local area;
•	A tool that will improve the lived experience of children and families, and support confidence in local SEND practices;
•	The Tool must be able to be ready for immediate implementation, with a proposed initiation date for use of October 2022.
 
